{
  "as_of": "2026-09-27",
  "scope": "Bounded XML 1.0 Fifth Edition and Namespaces in XML 1.0 admission for complete declared HTTP response representations. Simulated network peers, actual broker body/MCP paths and an isolated parser mutation audit; no deployment or external resource access.",
  "changes": [
    "Apply XML admission to application/xml, text/xml and structured +xml responses, including complete single ranges and complete representations assembled within one multipart response. Preserve accepted bytes and charge consumed rejected bytes.",
    "Recognize a single nested root, XML characters and Fifth Edition Unicode names, quoted attributes, processing instructions, comments, CDATA and UTF-8 XML declarations with position/order constraints.",
    "Enforce namespace declarations, restoration, reserved bindings, raw attribute uniqueness and expanded attribute uniqueness. Normalize only internal attribute values for namespace comparisons.",
    "Reject all DTD/entity declarations before any entity processing. Admit only predefined entities and valid numeric references; never fetch external resources or execute document content.",
    "Bound document bytes, nesting, attributes, name/markup/reference sizes and markup/reference units. Check the Python byte ceiling before decoding oversized direct inputs.",
    "For multipart representations declaring both JSON and XML, apply both contracts after proving full byte coverage. No new Snort SID was added."
  ],
